      "content": "that's a good start but it feels a bit one-sided. i mean, isn't there also a huge economic argument that migrant labor is actually what keeps the agricultural and service sectors stable? some people say strict enforcement actually hurts economic stability more than it helps. can u address that side of the debate too?",
