      "content": "while that makes sense, it feels like the \"national sovereignty\" piece is being treated as a secondary issue compared to the economic stuff. if the border isn't secure, doesn't that fundamentally undermine the very idea of a sovereign state, regardless of the economic perks? like, can you really have a stable economy if the state can't even control its own borders? it seems like a massive contradiction in the current policy approach.",
